# ~/.authinfo  — where the OpenRouter key lives on the machine
#
# This file is a *template*. The real one is NOT in this repo (it holds a
# secret) and must never be committed.
#
#   cp dotfiles/authinfo.example ~/.authinfo
#   chmod 600 ~/.authinfo
#   # then replace REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_KEY with your real key
#
# Key source: https://openrouter.ai/keys  (starts with sk-or-v1-)
#
# Field layout — auth-source only needs `machine' + `password'; the rest is
# convention. This exact shape is what this config was verified against:
#
machine openrouter.ai login apikey password REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_KEY
#
# Who reads it:
#   * gptel   — config.el sets `:key #'gptel-api-key-from-auth-source'
#   * minuet  — reads the same key at load time and exports
#               OPENROUTER_API_KEY into the process environment
# Nothing else in this config touches your secrets.
#
# Optional hardening: `gpg -c ~/.authinfo` produces ~/.authinfo.gpg, which
# auth-source/epa reads transparently. Delete the plaintext file afterwards.
